+{
+ "cells": [
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "`Perc` replaces observations with percentile values. By default, it computes five evenly spaced levels from 0 to 100, giving the minimum, quartiles, and maximum. An integer `k` requests a different number of evenly spaced levels; a list gives explicit levels. Each output row records its level in `percentile`.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The default method is `linear`. NumPy also supports `inverted_cdf`, `averaged_inverted_cdf`, `closest_observation`, `interpolated_inverted_cdf`, `hazen`, `weibull`, `median_unbiased`, `normal_unbiased`, `lower`, `higher`, `midpoint`, and `nearest`."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "import pandas as pd\n",
+    "import seaborn.objects as so\n",
+    "\n",
+    "data = pd.DataFrame({\"group\": [\"a\"] * 5, \"value\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]})\n",
+    "so.Plot(data, x=\"group\", y=\"value\").add(so.Dots(), so.Perc())"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Choose a count or explicit percentile levels with `k`:"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "so.Plot(data, x=\"group\", y=\"value\").add(so.Dots(), so.Perc(k=3))\n",
+    "so.Plot(data, x=\"group\", y=\"value\").add(so.Dots(), so.Perc(k=[10, 50, 90]))"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Combine `Perc` with a range mark to draw the interval between two percentiles:"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "so.Plot(data, x=\"group\", y=\"value\").add(so.Range(), so.Perc(k=[25, 75]))"
+   ]
+  }
